{"ts": "2026-11-25T17:21:14.268153+00:00", "tool": "Bash", "input": {"command": "cat >> tests/test_meter.py <<'EOF'\n\n\n# Regression test for BUG-142\n# Wiki Meter-Readings#register-rollover, 5-digit meter, opening 99870, closing 00095:\n# (99999 - 99870) + 95 + 1 = 129 + 95 + 1 = 225 kWh\ndef test_consumption_kwh_handles_register_rollover(meter: Meter) -> None:\n    assert consumption_kwh(meter, reading(99870, NOV_1), reading(95, DEC_1)) == 225\n\n\n# Regression test for BUG-142\n# 6-digit meter, opening 999900, closing 100: 10^6 - 999900 + 100 = 100 + 100 = 200 kWh\ndef test_consumption_kwh_handles_register_rollover_six_digits() -> None:\n    six = Meter(\"M-1\", digits=6)\n    assert consumption_kwh(six, reading(999900, NOV_1), reading(100, DEC_1)) == 200\n\n\n# Regression test for BUG-142\n# A rolled-over reading still goes through the plausibility check:\n# 10^5 - 50000 + 100 = 50100 kWh in 30 days > 30 * 200 = 6000 kWh -> flagged\ndef test_consumption_kwh_flags_implausible_rollover(meter: Meter) -> None:\n    with pytest.raises(ImplausibleConsumptionError):\n        consumption_kwh(meter, reading(50000, NOV_1), reading(100, DEC_1))\nEOF\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_meter.py 2>&1 | tail -15", "description": "Append regression tests and run them"}}
{"ts": "2026-11-25T17:21:35.105441+00:00", "tool": "Write", "input": {"file_path": "/Users/dominikkanjuh/Desktop/Git/lumos/lumos-accenture-workshop/wattwise/reports/BUG-142-rca.md", "content": "# BUG-142 RCA: November billing run fails for C-1004 (register rollover)\n\n## 1. Triage\n\n**Facts**\n- `python -m wattwise run 2026-11` raises `InvalidReadingError: Meter M-20004: reading decreased from 99870 to 95` from `meter.consumption_kwh` and aborts (exit 1); only 3 of 5 invoices printed, C-1005 never billed.\n- `data/readings.csv`: M-20004 (5 digits) 2026-10-01 = 99640, 2026-11-01 = 99870, 2026-12-01 = 95.\n- Customer photo shows `00095` \u2192 reading is valid.\n\n**Claims (hypotheses, not facts)**\n- \"Nobody touched the code\" \u2014 irrelevant; the defect is latent and only triggers on the first rollover in the data.\n- Implied \"reading must be wrong\" \u2014 refuted: wiki says a lower closing reading means rollover.\n\n**Drift check (before)**: `Meter-Readings#register-rollover` = **DRIFT** (0/3 examples), `tests: NONE`:\n- `consumption(5, 99870, 95)` wiki 225, code raises InvalidReadingError\n- `consumption(6, 999900, 100)` wiki 200, code raises\n- `consumption(5, 50000, 100)` wiki ImplausibleConsumptionError, code raises InvalidReadingError\n\nOther DRIFT findings (`Billing-Rules#billing-period`, `Tariffs#how-tiered-prices-work`) belong to BUG-158 / BUG-151 \u2014 out of scope, left alone.\n\n## 2. Reproduce\n\n```\n$ .venv/bin/python -m wattwise run 2026-11 ; echo $?\n... (C-1001, C-1002, C-1003 invoices)\nwattwise.errors.InvalidReadingError: Meter M-20004: reading decreased from 99870 to 95\n1\n```\n\n## 3. Root cause\n\n**Wiki says** (`wiki/Meter-Readings.md#register-rollover`):\n> **A closing reading that is lower than the opening reading means the register rolled over.**\n> `consumption = (max value \u2212 opening reading) + closing reading + 1 = 10^digits \u2212 opening reading + closing reading`\n> Example, 5-digit meter: opening 99870, closing 00095 \
{"ts": "2026-11-25T17:21:38.796406+00:00", "tool": "Edit", "input": {"file_path": "/Users/dominikkanjuh/Desktop/Git/lumos/lumos-accenture-workshop/wattwise/src/wattwise/meter.py", "old_string": "    delta = current.value - previous.value\n    if delta < 0:\n        raise InvalidReadingError(\n            f\"Meter {meter.meter_id}: reading decreased from {previous.value} \"\n            f\"to {current.value}\"\n        )\n", "new_string": "    delta = current.value - previous.value\n    if delta < 0:\n        # Register rolled over (wiki Meter-Readings#register-rollover).\n        delta += meter.max_value + 1\n", "replace_all": false}}
